From c80f71431b21daad836c865b5e54351b2f949fc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Melhede <95473109+AMelhede@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rppg-web): pulse check rule screenLight, a window one
 light steps on the whole face is not evidence

A face with no pulse lit by a screen showing video was read as a heart rate:
one light moves forehead and both cheeks together, so the regions agree on
whatever rhythm the screen happens to have. Blood cannot make a step; a
screen cut, a switched lamp or an exposure change scales all the skin by
the same share in one frame.

A 16 s window holding 10 or more equal light steps (same direction, the
smallest over max(1%, 0.4/s x frame gap), the largest at most 1.35 x the
smallest, frames under 250 ms apart, each new level holding for 100 ms,
consecutive frames easing one change in counted once) cannot count toward
the proof. The brightness floor that discards a lost face is read on
either value scale (0 to 1 or 0 to 255). On by default; it only withholds,
never makes or changes a rate. pulseCheckRules.screenLight: false restores
the previous behaviour. The state gains windowScreenSteps and screenLight.

Still missed: slow (steps 1 to 3 s apart) or shallow (5%) screen changes.
